# Integrations

## Pattern (every provider)

```
apps/api/src/integrations/<capability>/
├── <capability>.port.ts          interface the services depend on (e.g. PaymentGateway)
├── providers/<provider>.ts       real implementation
├── providers/fake.ts             in-memory fake used by tests and local dev when no keys
├── <capability>.module.ts        picks the provider from env
└── <capability>.spec.ts          contract tests run against the fake (and the sandbox when keys exist)
```

Services depend on the port, never on a provider SDK, so swapping providers touches one folder.

## Rules

- Config from env, validated at boot; sandbox/test keys in development; `.env.example` documents every variable. Missing keys → the fake provider plus a startup warning, so the build keeps moving.
- Outbound calls: timeouts, retries with exponential backoff and jitter for idempotent operations only, circuit-breaker style fail-fast when a provider is down, and queueing (background jobs) for anything slow such as emails, SMS, PDFs and exports.
- Inbound webhooks: verify signature, timestamp window, de-duplicate by event ID, process idempotently, respond fast and do the work in a job.
- Payments: server computes amounts; idempotency keys; order confirmed only by a verified callback/webhook, never by the browser redirect.
- Never log full payloads containing personal or payment data; store provider IDs, not card data.
- Never call real third-party endpoints from tests or from red-team runs; use the fake or the provider's sandbox.

## Common choices (verify current options and pricing at decision time)

| Capability | Typical options | Local dev |
|---|---|---|
| Email | SMTP, Resend, Postmark, Amazon SES | Mailpit on :{{MAIL_PORT}} (UI :{{MAIL_UI_PORT}}) |
| SMS / OTP | Twilio or a local-market SMS gateway | Fake provider logging to console |
| Payments | Stripe internationally; regional gateways where needed (for Bangladesh, e.g. SSLCommerz or bKash) | Provider sandbox |
| File storage | S3-compatible (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2) | MinIO container |
| PDF / QR (tickets, receipts) | Server-side PDF and QR libraries | Same |
| Calendar | ICS file generation | Same |
| Push notifications | Expo push / FCM / APNs | Fake provider |

Record each chosen provider, why, and its env variables in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and the PRD integrations section.
